<title>FRANCE: PSA sees 9-10 pct French car market fall in 1997.</title>
<headline>PSA sees 9-10 pct French car market fall in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>PSA Peugeot Citroen chairman Jacques Calvet said on Wednesday he saw the car market falling by nine or 10 percent in France in 1997.</p>
<p>He predicted the market would remain stable in Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;...the French market in 1997 should be around the same size as the market in 1995, which means 1.93 million cars or a fall of nine to 10 percent from 1996,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
